---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import SectionHeading from "../../components/SectionHeading.astro";
import SafetyNotice from "../../components/SafetyNotice.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="How Local Flight Connects"
  description="See what Local Flight keeps on your home network, when it uses the internet, what each optional service sends, and how Companion, Remote Companion, and Standalone differ."
  active="network"
>
  <header class="terminal-hero">
    <div class="terminal-frame terminal-grid hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow">How It Connects / Local and online paths</div>
        <h1 class="hero-title">Most of Local Flight <span class="accent-word">stays on your network.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Your screens talk to the computer running Local Flight over your home or local network (LAN). The internet is used only for the flight data you choose, phone-only Standalone mode, optional encrypted access away from home, or a report you submit.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="action-button action-button--primary" href="#paths">See every connection <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a class="action-link" href="/privacy/">Read the privacy policy</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual">
        <div class="network-terminal" aria-label="Local Flight connection summary" data-reveal>
          <div class="network-terminal-head"><span>PATH</span><span>DESTINATION</span><span>STATE</span></div>
          <div><b>AT HOME</b><span>Your computer and screens</span><i>LOCAL</i></div>
          <div><b>FLIGHT DATA</b><span>Your chosen source</span><i>CHOICE</i></div>
          <div><b>AWAY</b><span>Encrypted paired messages</span><i>OPTIONAL</i></div>
          <div><b>REPORTS</b><span>Only when sent or enabled</span><i>CONSENT</i></div>
          <p>Illustrative connection table · no live network inspection</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" id="paths">
    <div class="terminal-frame">
      <SectionHeading index="01 / CONNECTIONS" title="Follow only the paths your setup uses." description="Each path below says what connects and what leaves your device. Local screens stay local; optional online services enter only for the feature you select." />
      <div class="connection-diagram" data-reveal>
        <div class="connection-lane">
          <strong>Use Local Flight around the house</strong><span class="connection-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="connection-stop"><strong>Computer running Local Flight</strong><span>Windows · macOS · Linux · Raspberry Pi</span></div>
          <span class="connection-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="connection-stop"><strong>Your local screens</strong><span>Desktop app · browser · LED matrix · Companion. Nothing leaves your network for this connection.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="connection-lane">
          <strong>Get real-world flight data</strong><span class="connection-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="connection-stop"><strong>Your own aviation-data API keys</strong><span>The keys remain saved on the computer running Local Flight.</span></div>
          <span class="connection-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="connection-stop"><strong>Your selected provider</strong><span>Only the provider receives its key and the airport or aircraft request needed for the feature.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="connection-lane connection-lane--optional">
          <strong>Use the Beacon Tools shared service</strong><span class="connection-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="connection-stop"><strong>Your Local Flight setup</strong><span>Sends a random service ID and the airport request needed for the shared board.</span></div>
          <span class="connection-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="connection-stop"><strong>Community Relay</strong><span>Reuses recent shared airport data and applies update and fair-use limits.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="connection-lane connection-lane--optional">
          <strong>Reach your setup while away</strong><span class="connection-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="connection-stop"><strong>Remote Companion</strong><span>The encryption key stays on your paired phone and Local Flight computer.</span></div>
          <span class="connection-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="connection-stop"><strong>Community Relay</strong><span>Passes along encrypted messages and routing details. Beacon Tools cannot read the message.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="connection-lane connection-lane--optional">
          <strong>Use only a phone</strong><span class="connection-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="connection-stop"><strong>Standalone</strong><span>Your airport choice and recent movement history remain on the phone.</span></div>
          <span class="connection-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="connection-stop"><strong>Community Relay</strong><span>Receives a random service ID and the requests needed for board, radar, weather, and map data.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--quiet section--ruled">
    <div class="terminal-frame">
      <SectionHeading index="02 / UPDATE TIMING" title="Why Local Flight may keep showing an older board." description="Aviation-data services have update limits and can be temporarily unavailable. Local Flight keeps a known board visible when it is safer and more useful than an empty screen, and shows when the data was last updated." />
      <div class="cadence-line" data-reveal>
        <article class="cadence-item"><strong>30 min</strong><h3>Community Relay board</h3><p>A Community Relay setup requests a new schedule board no more often than every 30 minutes.</p></article>
        <article class="cadence-item"><strong>About 1 h</strong><h3>Standalone Board</h3><p>Airline schedules usually refresh about once an hour. Shared information may still be cached or delayed.</p></article>
        <article class="cadence-item"><strong>About 3 min</strong><h3>Standalone Radar</h3><p>Nearby traffic can refresh about every 3 minutes while Radar is open.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-footnote" style="margin-top: 28px">Between schedule checks, Standalone re-evaluates its saved real-world board locally without requesting new airline data. VATSIM Standalone targets about one-minute board and Radar checks. If a provider has a temporary problem, Local Flight may keep the last known board visible—check the freshness time shown in the app.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="terminal-frame">
      <SectionHeading index="03 / TROUBLESHOOTING" title="Start with the mode shown in the app." description="The mode name tells you whether to check your home network, the computer running Local Flight, or the phone’s internet connection." />
      <ol class="troubleshooting-list" data-reveal>
        <li><span class="step">01 / HOME</span><strong>Companion on Wi-Fi</strong><p>Keep the phone and Local Flight computer on the same trusted network, confirm Local Flight is running, and scan the pairing code in Settings or enter the local address with port <code>:8000</code>.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step">02 / AWAY</span><strong>Remote Companion</strong><p>Leave the Local Flight computer online and connected to Community Relay. If access was revoked, return to the same home or local network and pair again.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step">03 / DIRECT</span><strong>Standalone</strong><p>Check the phone’s internet connection and wait a few minutes. A recent board may remain visible while a provider is unavailable.</p></li>
        <li><span class="step">04 / SUPPORT</span><strong>Need another pair of eyes?</strong><p>Use <a href="/support/">Support</a> and include the mode, airport, approximate time, and whether the phone and Local Flight computer were online. Include diagnostics only if you choose.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SafetyNotice subject="Relay responses and cached board, radar, weather, and map data" />
</SiteLayout>
